Archmechanic Hogan Voss Darkmoor, of the Darkmoors, is the man the [[Org/The Harlequins/index|Harlequins]] named as most likely to lead to the [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]] Rapid Connection, and so to keystone 14. The Party learned his name from the harlequin who set the three-question game at the [[Geography/Calaria/Ragged Roost|Ragged Roost]] pilgrimage, and none of them had heard of him before.

He is a little under six feet tall and wears the Org's orange robes, his face hidden behind a metal mask that his lower jaw works through, with a tube running from the side of the mouth to a backpack like the other servitors'. Rods of dull metal run in his neck and arms; one hand has eight mechanical fingers and two thumbs worked by pneumatics, and the other is a mount that takes a pen or another implement, which he swaps as he needs. His voice comes through the mask undistorted, unlike the static of his staff's radios.

He keeps a plain office on the second floor of the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus|Sub Transit Nexus]], with a desk holding only a pen, an inkwell and a small plaque, and a guest couch that looks never to have been used. He had not been down to the fane in close to seventy years, since he took the post, and says it is hard for him to leave the building for long, since the trains of Prime Meridian would stop. He takes all his food as IV packs.

[[Org/Prime Meridian/Rapid Connection|Rapid Connection]] speaks through his mask when it wishes, and he can drive the bodies of the workers in the building as a puppeteer would; he cannot fight himself, being a civilian.
